    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d854">

                <pb facs="0789" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/322.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the General
                        Receiver</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Government stated to German Ambassador in July last that its intention was
                    to cause the General Receiver to designate Monrovia as residence of German
                    Receiver. Nothing was said as to duration of such designation. The French
                    Government now asks that receivers be successively assigned for fixed periods to
                    Monrovia, the receiver at which place is to assume the duties of General
                    Receiver when the latter is absent. This seems equitable, and the subject of <pb
                        facs="0790" n="674" xml:id="pg674"/> giving the German Receiver the first
                    term at Monrovia can probably be worked out in due course through consultation
                    of the four Governments with the Government of Liberia. This must be discreetly
                    handled and should be arranged after you have been some time at Monrovia and the
                    whole arrangement and the receivership has been installed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
